# The `remove-dev-envs` tool: delete the cloud environments `caos-stack start
# --cloud-env` made, which nothing else cleans up. Run it by hand now and then:
#
#   caos-cli run-tool dev/remove-dev-envs
#
# A std/go worker that drives `drive` (design/daemons.md). It is `dev/` and not
# `std/` because it is for the people who run dev stacks, not for an agent.
#
# IT NEEDS THE TREE PUBLISHED. `drive` is granted the claude-oauth-token by origin,
# and the grant matches only a walk whose root tree is one `caosd up` published as
# refs/caos/dev on this stack. After editing the tree, `nix build && caosd up` first,
# or `drive` answers "no token at /secret/claude-oauth-token". This is true of every
# tool that calls `drive`, `caos-stack --cloud-env` included.
#
# Nothing is bound but the images: it takes no arguments and `at`, which every
# `drive` verb needs, is made by the worker itself.
HELP=<<END
Delete every cloud environment whose name starts with "z Caos Dev ", which is what
`caos-stack start --cloud-env` creates for each stack. Environments with any other
name are left alone. Returns the names it deleted, or says there were none.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --drive:@=DEEP-DEPS/drive --help=$HELP
